    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered account of what happens on `POST /api/owners`, reading the pipeline in `owners.POST.yml` and each function class. Every step runs inside a single write transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]`), so the whole thing commits once at the end.\n\n## Gate (before the pipeline)\n\n0. **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Caller lacking `OWNER_ADMIN` is denied (`AuthorizationDeniedException`) before any step runs.\n\n## Pipeline steps, in order\n\n1. **`CheckIdempotencyKey`** *(side-effect / short-circuit)* \u2014 If an `Idempotency-Key` header is present, non-blank, previously recorded, and still resolves to an existing owner, it **short-circuits**: responds `200 OK` with the original owner and never enters the create path. Otherwise takes the `proceed` branch. (This is also the only place the body is *not* yet read.)\n\n2. **`NormalizeAddress`** *(side-effect; reads the body)* \u2014 The single `@RequestBody` step. Normalizes the address (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand abbreviations). Prefers structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` when `addressLine1` is non-blank, composing them into the flat `address`; otherwise normalizes the flat `address`. Republishes the request for later steps.\n\n3. **`RequireOwnerFields`** *(validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 Rejects if any mandatory field is blank after normalization: `firstName`, `lastName`, address (blank in *both* `addressLine1` and `address`), `city`, `telephone`. Throws `MissingOwnerFieldsException`.\n\n4. **`RejectFutureRegistrationDate`** *(validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 If `registrationDate` is supplied and is after the server's current date, throws `FutureRegistrationDateException`. Absent date is allowed.\n\n5. **`ValidatePostcode`** *(validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 If `postcode` present, must be exactly 4 digits; and for a city with a known region (via `Locality`) must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Throws `InvalidPostcodeException`. Absent/blank postcode allowed; unknown region accepts any 4-digit code.\n\n6. **`NormalizeTelephone`** *(side-effect + validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 Normalizes `telephone` to E.164 (defaults country code `+61`, drops a leading `0`, strips separators, requires 8\u201315 digits), writing it back. Unformattable numbers throw `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n\n7. **`NormalizeEmail`** *(side-effect + validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 If `email` present, must be syntactically valid; trims and lower-cases it back onto the request. Invalid throws `InvalidEmailException`. Absent/blank allowed.\n\n8. **`RejectDisposableEmailDomain`** *(validation \u2192 400)* \u2014 If `email` present and its domain is on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), throws `DisposableEmailDomainException`.\n\n9. **`RejectDuplicateOwner`** *(validation \u2192 409)* \u2014 Household duplicate check: rejects if any non-soft-deleted existing owner shares the same `HouseholdId` (derived from `lastName` + `postcode`). Throws `DuplicateIdentityException`. **Bypassed** when the request sets `sharesHousehold = true`.\n\n10. **`RejectCityAtCapacity`** *(validation \u2192 409)* \u2014 Rejects if the request's city (matched case-insensitively, whitespace-collapsed) already has \u2265 50 owners. Throws `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n11. **`RejectOverDailyLimit`** *(validation \u2192 429)* \u2014 Computes the effective registration day (supplied or today, rolled forward off weekends to Monday). Rejects if \u2265 100 existing owners already have that `registrationDate`. Throws `DailyLimitExceededException`.\n\n12. **`BuildOwner`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Maps the request DTO to a new `Owner` entity; defaults `registrationDate` to today if absent, then business-day-adjusts it (weekend \u2192 next Monday).\n\n13. **`AssignCustomerCode`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Sets `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>`, REGION from `Locality` (postcode range \u2192 city table \u2192 `UNKNOWN`), HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex chars of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`. On collision with an existing code, appends `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2).\n\n14. **`AssignMembershipNumber`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Sets `membershipNumber = <customerCode>-M<YY>`, YY = last two digits of the fiscal year (starting 1 July) of the adjusted `registrationDate`.\n\n15. **`CountNamesakes`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Sets `namesakeCount` to the number of existing owners with the same first + last name (case-insensitive).\n\n16. **`CountHousehold`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Sets `householdSize` to existing owners sharing the same `HouseholdId`, plus 1 (this owner).\n\n17. **`AssignMembershipLevel`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Computes `membershipPoints`: +2 for having an email, +1 if `namesakeCount == 0`, +2 if `householdSize \u2265 3`, +3 if tenure \u2265 1 elapsed fiscal year. Maps points to `membershipLevel` 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (\u22656). Sets both.\n\n18. **`FlagBulkSignup`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if more than 80 existing owners already share this owner's registration day, else false.\n\n19. **`DetectPossibleDuplicate`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 If `sharesHousehold = true`, sets `possibleDuplicate = false`, `possibleDuplicateOf = null`. Otherwise, if any non-soft-deleted existing owner shares the `HouseholdId`, sets `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = lowest matching owner id; else false/null.\n\n20. **`SaveOwner`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns the id).\n\n21. **`RecordIdempotencyKey`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 If an `Idempotency-Key` header was supplied, records `key \u2192 new owner id` in the `IdempotencyStore` for future replays.\n\n22. **`AuditOwnerCreated`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Logs an audit line to the `AUDIT` logger with the new id, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, `membershipLevel`, `membershipNumber`.\n\n23. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** *(side-effect / response)* \u2014 Maps to `OwnerDto` and responds `201 Created` with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes on ordering that matter\n\n- **Validation precedes mutation/persistence**: all reject/require checks (steps 3\u201311) run before the entity is built or saved, and all share the transaction \u2014 so a rejection commits nothing.\n- **Normalization happens before the checks that depend on it** \u2014 address before the required-field check; telephone/email normalization before the customer-code hash and disposable-domain check.\n- **All \"count existing owners\" steps (9, 10, 11, 13, 15, 16, 18, 19, and the code-collision check in 13) run before `SaveOwner`**, so `findAll()` sees only pre-existing owners, not the one being created.\n- The `sharesHousehold` flag relaxes exactly two things: the hard duplicate block (step 9) and the soft-duplicate flag (step 19).\n\nI read the code only; nothing was changed."
